-- copies/6345850877-1.md --
verdict: approve-with-conditions
Before adding ADRs 0010-0016, resolve the record-placement conflict under R10 with a decision note or ADR and update the affected guidance in the same change. The plan puts tally-specific build, package, parser and counting decisions in docs/adr/, while docs/adr/README.md, “What belongs in this directory”, restricts that directory to constitutive records “generic enough to carry onto any domain”. docs/engineering-discipline.md, “Architecture Decision Records”, also directs architecturally significant structure and interface decisions there. Make the permitted home for these product decisions explicit; do not silently bypass the restriction.
The seven selected options all survive their supplied constraint filters. The cmd/tally layout and unicode.IsSpace selections include reasons for choosing between surviving alternatives; the remaining selections have one survivor each. The choices support REQ-001 through REQ-017 and NFR-018 through NFR-024 without adding product scope or external dependencies.
The four fields and empty tests: list satisfy the architecture plan form. No implementation tests are required in this task. Preserve the existing blank MoSCoW and Phase cells and existing facts records; the plan correctly promises no Go code or new facts record.
At plan scope, the selected technical approach has one reading; the record-placement conflict above is the condition to resolve before execution. This review approves architecture and scope only, not implementation correctness or performance.
-- copies/6347751487-1.md --
head: c17c28c8c9c3578056f960aa98ba907bfbd15fc7
verdict: material
findings:
- docs/tasks/T-am8b.md:43 R12: The supplied plan explicitly selects cmd-tally-count-subpackage and unicode-isspace, and its independent review approves both selections with only a record-placement condition. This change instead defers both choices to the bet, omits their ADRs, and introduces a rule prohibiting selection when multiple options survive. Multiple survivors do not invalidate the reviewed choices. Restore the selected architecture and its decision records, or record an authorized plan revision before treating the replacement scope as approved.
- docs/adr/0013-parse-flags-by-hand.md:23 R13: The unconditional rule classifies every multi-character argument starting with a hyphen as a flag group, including arguments after a filename, while lines 38-40 explicitly leave that case for the idea owner. Thus tally file -l is both specified as selecting lines and declared unresolved; SPEC-0002 step 1 repeats the unconditional rule. Limit the decision to the supported argument positions and explicitly preserve the unresolved case, or obtain a fact resolving it, so the architecture gives one instruction to the implementer.
-- copies/6347893425-1.md --
head: 0ebf7d9e0f4f91881cce4d1368c9e62826fcc98a
verdict: material
findings:
- docs/tasks/T-am8b.md:49 R12: The supplied plan selects cmd-tally-count-subpackage and unicode-isspace, and its independent review approves both subject only to resolving record placement. This paragraph asserts an operator instruction reversing those selections, but no such instruction or confirmation is present in the supplied issue, plan, answers or handoffs; it explicitly leaves confirmation pending. The architecture still defers both reviewed choices and omits their ADRs. Restore the selected architecture and records, or supply the authorized revision and record its confirmation on the issue before treating the replacement scope as approved.
- docs/adr/README.md:20 R10: The record-placement resolution adds product ADRs but retains the rule that records cite only sibling constitutive documents. ADR-0010 instead requires citations of the product PRD and specification, and ADR-0011 through ADR-0015 use those citations. Thus the guidance still both prohibits and requires the new records' product references. Update this rule to explicitly permit product requirements and specifications, consistent with ADR-0010, so the plan review's record-placement condition is fully resolved.
